SI-3 stage 4 (SI3-4): the sixty-two legacy assignment statements deleted

Zero module-level _<STEM>_(BASE|SEALED_HEAD|MERGE) statements remain in
the guard file, by SI2-6(b)'s own extraction, which is kept as the
standing detector. R7-RNT's clause-9 block, reduced at stage 3 to its
two rebindings, probe and restore lines, goes as a block here: its two
rebindings were two of the sixty-two, and the probe and restore lines
read names that no longer exist. SI2-6(b), LEGACY-INTACT, is retired
per the supersession table and now prints the head's statement count.

Dry run at this stage, taken before stage 5 as the freeze orders
(stage 5 has no all-PASS precondition): 91 PASS, one FAIL -- R7-SI2 on
SI2-4 alone, DELTA-BROKEN with 0 of 23 records agreeing and the census
artifact reported STALE, because U4's old side transcribes the head's
guard text and the head now carries no constant. SI2-3, SI2-5 and
SI2-6(a) (MAP-PRESERVED, 91 base tags identical) all held. R7-SI1
passed entire, SI1-5 included: its harness runs the generic archive
helpers on each record's own fields and never read a constant, so the
SI-1 census still reproduced after the deletion; recorded for the
result note, since the freeze's stated reason for retiring SI1-5 was
that its old side read the constants.
